WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.018
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie. This is gonna be my Arrow episode 21 video.

00:00:04.018 --> 00:00:09.891
Lots of comicbook stuff we have to work through, including the person that might end up being the season 4 villain.

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:12.757
Just this big rumor that was going around a couple of months ago

00:00:12.757 --> 00:00:16.806
was that the finale would tee up who the season 4 villain is going to be

00:00:16.806 --> 00:00:18.893
and they basically called him out in this episode

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:22.055
so careful for spoilers if you haven't seen 21 yet

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:27.175
Starting with top 5 moments. Number 5: meet Damien Darhk, probably gonna be the Arrow season 4 villain.

00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:34.623
So, as Rha's Al Ghul was like slowly brain washing and training Oliver using the fear toxin from Batman Begins no less

00:00:34.623 --> 00:00:38.563
he explains that Damien Darhk was a person who joined the League the same time he did

00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:45.323
but ended up hopping on the crazy train and created a splinter organization to carry on the League's work as he saw it

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:50.210
Rha's tasks Oliver with taking Damien down. This is just the beginning.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.267
Damien Darhk is actually a character from the Teen Titans comics. 

00:00:53.277 --> 00:00:56.530
I know everyone always asks about the Titan show that's happening on TNT

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.752
They've actually changed the name of that show, it's not called Titans anymore, but I'll talk about it in another video.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.080
Damien debuted in Titans nº1 in 1999

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.279
He really only existed inside that arc, it was like a 12 issue arc

00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:11.760
So, in issue number 12 he ended up being killed by Vandal Savage

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.660
He hasn't appeared in the new 52 comics

00:01:14.692 --> 00:01:19.812
But he is a big H.I.V.E. character and he gets tied up with Slade Wilson's wife

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:24.393
Her name is Adeline Kane so, if they're gonna be doing Damien Darhk-H.I.V.E. in season 4

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.180
it'd be an easy way to bring Deathstroke back on the show

00:01:28.183 --> 00:01:31.740
and they said they can do that. Even though the Suicide Squad movie might be doing Deathstroke

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.299
they can still put him on the show, they can still bring Manu Bennett

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:40.679
So they tie Damien Darhk to all these past events on the show, like trying to buy the prototype of Merlyn's earthquake machine

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:42.308
and killing Diggle's brother

00:01:42.308 --> 00:01:44.727
They'll continue to do that, and what I'm hoping that they do

00:01:44.727 --> 00:01:48.389
is that they tie him to Felicity, he ends up being Felicity's father

00:01:48.389 --> 00:01:50.616
In the comics, Damien's known for his baby-face

00:01:50.616 --> 00:01:52.698
I don't know how the show's going to address this, because

00:01:52.698 --> 00:01:56.074
supposedly only Rha's Al Ghul has access to Lazarus pit

00:01:56.074 --> 00:02:01.469
So we might see the same kind of thing going on with Damien, he might just be like a really old person in a young person's body

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:05.626
Moving on to number 4: Oliver-League of Assassins training montage

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:10.151
I really like the way they shot the opening scene, just like cutting over the course of a couple weeks

00:02:10.151 --> 00:02:15.492
Oliver slowly gets brainwashed with the fear toxin, and gets really badass with swords

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.040
They're not only brainwashing him, they're also training him to fight

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.802
Even though Team Arrow seemed like they'd almost given up on him by the end of the episode

00:02:21.802 --> 00:02:24.932
there is no programming that cannot be broken somehow

00:02:24.932 --> 00:02:27.991
Something is going to happen to redeem him at a certain point

00:02:27.991 --> 00:02:30.320
Whether or not they carry it into season 4 we have no idea

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.910
I always like how they try to trip you up with like an opening moment WTF

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:37.782
like him stabbing Diggle, but then it turns out it's someone else

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:40.984
Great way to start an episode, make everyone poop their pants

00:02:40.984 --> 00:02:44.474
On to number 3: Laurel and Nyssa are milkshake gal pals

00:02:44.474 --> 00:02:47.553
I really like the way they developed a friendship between those two characters

00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:51.226
Nyssa is such an awesome character so I'm just happy to have her on the show

00:02:51.226 --> 00:02:57.575
I think it's a good way to humanize her and give Laurel a really nice arc that has absolutely nothing to do with the rest of the team Arrow

00:02:57.575 --> 00:02:59.625
Like they can just have their own scenes off on their own

00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:02.678
Mostly Nyssa trying to train her the same way she trained Sara

00:03:02.678 --> 00:03:05.956
That's gonna take a long time but now that she has the canary cry

00:03:05.956 --> 00:03:08.896
I think she'll learn to use that, too, and it'll help close some of that distance

00:03:08.896 --> 00:03:12.042
It's just really interesting dichotomy they had between Oliver and Nyssa

00:03:12.042 --> 00:03:16.649
Whereby, she slowly gains her humanity and Oliver is like losing his at the same time

00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:19.638
It's too bad they captured her at the end of the episode, because

00:03:19.638 --> 00:03:22.874
I was kind of hoping she'd join team Arrow, like the new team Arrow for a little while

00:03:22.874 --> 00:03:26.328
I definitely have to give Laurel props though for being the voice of reason

00:03:26.328 --> 00:03:29.264
It's like everybody is losing their shit except for Laurel

00:03:29.264 --> 00:03:32.149
She's kind of like the moral conscience of team Arrow right now

00:03:32.149 --> 00:03:36.112
Moving on to number 2 though: Oliver kidnaps Lyla and threatens her life

00:03:36.112 --> 00:03:39.784
I don't think we were ever in any danger of Oliver killing Lyla 

00:03:39.784 --> 00:03:43.922
but it's still really heartbreaking to see him go up against his Arrow bro, Diggle

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:49.472
Lyla had that really nice speech about how joining team Arrow helped humanize Diggle

00:03:49.472 --> 00:03:52.021
Like after the war he was suffering from post traumatic stress

00:03:52.021 --> 00:03:54.274
but Oliver helped give him a purpose

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.820
It seems like it's all falling on deaf ears right now

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:02.266
but, I think at a certain point something will happen to shock Oliver back to consciousness 

00:04:02.266 --> 00:04:05.046
and if you're wondering, all those team Arrow scenes where they were meeting

00:04:05.046 --> 00:04:06.440
that was inside Ray Palmer's lab

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.704
That's gonna be like the temporary Arrow cave

00:04:08.704 --> 00:04:10.957
You can call it the ATOM cave if you want

00:04:10.957 --> 00:04:13.386
Eventually Ray will step in and help out

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.720
but he wasn't really necessary for this episode

00:04:16.226 --> 00:04:19.586
It was mostly about classic OG team Arrow vs Oliver

00:04:19.586 --> 00:04:25.489
And of course, my number 1 WTF moment: Rha's Al Ghul tells Nyssa that she is now the bride of the Demon

00:04:25.962 --> 00:04:29.162
and asks Oliver to unleash the Omega on Starling

00:04:29.162 --> 00:04:33.705
You can kind of see how we're drifting into Christopher Nolan-Batman territory here

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:35.887
"Destroy the city, wipe it clean"

00:04:35.887 --> 00:04:42.791
I like how he just casually dropped that the previous Rha's Al Ghul, his predecessor, wiped out Alexandria

00:04:42.837 --> 00:04:44.357
Like a biblical plague

00:04:44.357 --> 00:04:48.411
There was kind of a bible moment where he asks Oliver to kill Nyssa

00:04:48.411 --> 00:04:51.947
It was like when god asked Abraham to kill his son Isaac

00:04:51.947 --> 00:04:56.525
And then when he went in to do it, god stopped Abraham and said "No, this was just a test, and you passed"

00:04:56.525 --> 00:04:58.343
Bride of the Demon though, all I could think about

00:04:58.343 --> 00:05:04.598
was like the Bride of Frankenstein's scream when Elsa Lanchester just screams out loud with the crazy hair

00:05:04.598 --> 00:05:09.217
Mark Guggenheim did tease that there would be another wedding on Arrow this season

00:05:09.287 --> 00:05:10.647
that wasn't Diggle's

00:05:10.647 --> 00:05:15.138
I think we'll see some kind of ceremony, don't expect it to actually go down

00:05:15.138 --> 00:05:16.898
I don't think they'll make it to the vows

00:05:16.898 --> 00:05:18.925
Hopefully it'll actually go down in next week's episode

00:05:18.925 --> 00:05:20.298
that's what I'm looking forward to

00:05:20.298 --> 00:05:26.264
It's like, next week we deal with the wedding stuff and then the week after that, we deal with the Omega-Starling stuff

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:28.700
That really only scratches the surface of the episode

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.111
but here's my big question for you guys

00:05:30.111 --> 00:05:35.130
How do you think that team Arrow is going to help Oliver shake his programming?

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.349
Whatever they end up doing, it's gonna be something that they have to do together

00:05:38.349 --> 00:05:41.016
Like it'll be all of them together in the same moment

00:05:41.016 --> 00:05:46.819
If you remember in the mid-season finale, when Oliver died, all those images flashed through his brain

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:52.680
I wonder if the same type of thing is gonna happen, like what if he ended up dying and they dump him in the Lazarus pit

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.158
and he comes out changed

00:05:54.158 --> 00:05:57.182
that'd be pretty crazy. Remember, this last scene in this episode

00:05:57.182 --> 00:05:59.461
they were standing in front of the Lazarus pit

00:05:59.461 --> 00:06:03.999
So, I feel like the Lazarus pit is gonna continue to be a big plot point 

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:05.071
before season 4

00:06:05.071 --> 00:06:07.655
Somebody else needs to get dumped in there

